# Mobile
#
# The android/ folder USED to be ignored whole, on the reasoning that Capacitor
# regenerates it. It does - but it regenerates a STOCK project. It does not
# bring back the notification listener, the capture plugin, the payment filter,
# the manifest edits that register them, or the debug network-security config.
# All of that was hand-written, and none of it was in a single commit; it
# existed only on one laptop. So the source is tracked and only the genuinely
# generated parts are ignored.
/apps/web/android/build/
/apps/web/android/.gradle/
/apps/web/android/app/build/
# Absolute SDK path for one machine.
/apps/web/android/local.properties
# Written by `npx cap sync` from the plugins in package.json.
/apps/web/android/capacitor-cordova-android-plugins/
# The built web bundle, copied in by `npx cap sync` from apps/web/dist.
/apps/web/android/app/src/main/assets/public/
/apps/web/android/app/src/main/assets/capacitor.config.json
/apps/web/android/app/src/main/assets/capacitor.plugins.json

/apps/web/ios/
/apps/web/www/

# The release signing key and its password. Neither ever belongs in git: with
# both, anyone can publish an update that every existing install accepts as
# genuine. The .example file beside it is committed and holds no secret.
/apps/web/android/keystore.properties
*.jks
*.keystore
